---
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Therapies & clinical approach.

   ⚠ REBUILT after a verification pass. The earlier version published all
   eleven modalities from the client wiki as fact. Checked against the call
   export, only three have any supporting evidence:

     group therapy        7 calls
     individual therapy  12 calls
     step work / sponsor 28 calls   (not even on the wiki's list of eleven)

   Zero call evidence for: CBT, DBT, EMDR, family therapy, trauma-specific
   therapy, motivational interviewing, relapse prevention, life skills
   training. Holistic/meditation: 1.

   IMPORTANT CAVEAT — this is silence, not contradiction. Admissions calls are
   about getting someone through the door; nobody discusses EMDR protocol on an
   intake call. That is much weaker evidence than the IOP case, where agents
   explicitly denied having the service. These modalities may well be delivered.

   But the standing instruction is that the wiki is not trusted, so this page
   now publishes only what is corroborated and says plainly that the full
   clinical programme is described on the call. Restore any modality the
   clinical team confirms — and when they do, note who confirmed it here.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import HubHero from '../../components/hub/HubHero.astro';
import HubCards from '../../components/hub/HubCards.astro';
import Testimonials from '../../components/Testimonials.astro';
import VerifySection from '../../components/VerifySection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const title = 'Therapy & Clinical Approach | Buena Vista Health & Recovery, Chandler AZ';
const description = 'Group therapy twice daily, one-to-one sessions with your own therapist, and support for step work with your sponsor, inside residential treatment in Chandler, AZ. Call (888) 362-5576.';

const core = [
  { label: 'Group therapy', tag: 'Twice daily', desc: 'The backbone of the residential day, and the part most people are most nervous about beforehand. It is also the part they tend to name afterwards as the one that mattered.' },
  { label: 'Individual therapy', tag: 'One-to-one', desc: 'Sessions with your own therapist, working on what sits underneath rather than only on the substance itself.' },
  { label: 'Step work & your sponsor', tag: 'Encouraged', desc: 'If you have a sponsor they can come into the facility and do step work with you during your stay. If you do not, getting one is something the team will actively encourage.' },
  { label: 'Case management', tag: 'Throughout', desc: 'Someone working alongside you on what happens next — housing, a primary care provider, ongoing psychiatric care, and the practical scaffolding that makes leaving survivable.' },
];
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <TopBar /><Nav />
  <HubHero
    eyebrow="Therapy & clinical approach"
    title="The work happens in rooms with other people in them."
    intro="Residential treatment here is built around group therapy twice a day and one-to-one sessions with your own therapist, with a case manager working on what comes after from early in your stay."
    points={['Group therapy twice a day','Individual sessions with your own therapist','Sponsors welcome to come in and do step work','A case manager planning the next step from early on']}
    image="/Asset/stock%20photo/Desktop%20Dimensions/Facility/Intimate%20fireside%20lounge%20with%20four%20armchairs%20and%20built-in%20fireplace.png"
    alt="An intimate fireside lounge with four armchairs"
    caption="Where a lot of the real work happens."
  />

  <HubCards eyebrow="What your week is built around" title="The core of it" items={core} columns={4} />

  <section class="bg-sage-tint py-[70px]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
        Ask about the rest
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-5">Which specific therapies you would get</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-charcoal text-[17px] leading-[29px]">
        <p>
          Treatment programmes vary, and the specific modalities in your plan depend on what you actually need — what you have been using, what is going on mentally, and what has or has not worked for you before.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">Rather than list every technique on a website, we would rather tell you accurately.</strong> Ask on the admissions call, or ask your therapist in the first days, and you will get a straight answer about what your programme includes.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a particular approach matters to you — because it has helped before, or because someone recommended it — say so at the start. It is a reasonable thing to choose a programme on.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href="tel:8883625576" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-teal hover:bg-teal-dark text-white font-semibold h-14 px-8 rounded-lg transition-colors font-body">
          <span class="tel-number">Ask us — (888) 362-5576</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Testimonials /><VerifySection />
  <FinalCTA />
</Layout>
